[Music]  today is the day football fans around  the world have been waiting for when the  nfl debuts its 2022 season schedule our  friend bill cower from the nfl today  gave us a little preview earlier this  week revealing the denver broncos los  angeles rams matchup on christmas day  which will be a good one right here on  cbs but how exactly does the league  determine the full schedule when there  seems to be an endless combination of  opponents venues dates and bye weeks  earlier this week we took a trip to the  nfl offices here in new york city to  meet a very small but very vital team of  gridiron matchmakers  [Applause]  if you ever wondered how your favorite  team landed in snowy buffalo in december  this is just a wild scene in buffalo or  how the league somehow predicted that  perfect late season matchup here goes  you are not alone he hurdles and picks  up the first down  whoa the answers it turns out are far  more complicated than just sheer luck i  wonder how much of this  is still pretty much intact inside this  cramped room on manhattan's east side  mike north charlotte carey and ani bose  have been huddling for months you're  right i think we put new england mini in  there day one it may look like a college  freshman's dorm room but it has the feel  of something else altogether experience  north has been working this room for the  past quarter century and not too long  ago no computers no artificial  intelligence this was all done by hand  one game at a time yeah the miracle  isn't so much that we get through  hundreds of thousands of contenders  schedules today it's that we ever got  one done  by hand  it is truly remarkable every one of  these games can go in any one of now 18  weeks any one of seven networks any one  of ten different times you could put it  on sunday night you could put it on  monday night you can put it on sunday  afternoon you can put it in germany you  can put it on thanksgiving you can put  it on christmas you put in the first  half of the season you put in the second  half of the season  do that calculation for each of these  272 assets and you find real quickly  that you knew the computers were going  to do an infinitely better job than the  humans ever could doing it one game at a  time so let's break it down the league  has 32 teams each team plays 17 regular  season games  for a total of 272 contests  some in london this year a game in  germany one in mexico  then factor in weather travel distances  bye weeks broadcast partner needs  and scheduled stadium events so when i  walked in here i was expecting  it to look like an episode of homeland  we're talking focus points charts and  targets yarn strung together on faces of  different players and coaches  how do you not overload doing this job  it's long days and long nights and a  really long few months day after super  bowl we pretty much you know kind of  close and lock the door in here and  that's when we get started then go  through draft and uh then you know two  weeks later or so we put our schedule up  we we give the commissioner our best  schedule honestly we're not even done  yet nate so what it's still working  still it's still in progress broncos at  the rams christmas day yep the rams  coming off a super bowl matthew stafford  at quarterback russell wilson new bronco  that sounds like a football game those  are the games that are going to get the  most viewers and the most eyeballs and  you want to put them into the biggest  windows and spread them across all of  our partners so whether it's sunday  afternoon at 4 25 or monday night or  thursday night  you want to find that balance and then  in between all of that the the math is  the computers filling out the rest  the team told me they used thousands of  cloud-based computers to help narrow  down the potential trillions yes that's  right trillions of combinations to just  one single working schedule  it's so  incredible like the ramifications of  what happens in that room right people  plan birthday parties they plan parties  at their house they plan trips like when  that lands because of the work you just  showed lives change it's so true we're  talking bachelor parties weddings i mean  getaways they planted around the  football season and not to mention you  still have to make the players happy i  remember  and i didn't care about who we played or  if we were on prime time you were just  glad to play i was just glad to play and  i wanted warm weather games in the month  of december and january but other guys  they all had issues with certain parts  of the scheduling process which i did  not know i learned a lot because they  want prime time i like mr manbun what's  his name mike  mike mike i like you mike  has a new nickname he will no longer be  known as mike around his his man bun is  tight looks good but but the way all the  planning that goes into it and the way  he sort of laid it all out for you i  thought was really fascinating is i knew  they planned it but i had no idea it was  that detail they said imagine the  largest rubik's cube in your hand and  trying to figure it out all right that's  what it is all right the full 2022 nfl  schedule will be revealed tonight at 8  pm eastern on the nfl network and  paramount plus

